   the sustainability of protected areas. We undertook qualitative and
   ethnographic fieldwork to explore relationships between people and
   protected areas in the Blouberg mountain range, South Africa. The
   history of land use and current relationships with protected areas
   reveal legacies of marginalisation and immiseration, giving credence to
   a theory of traumatic nature. The impacts of traumatic nature manifest
   themselves in local discourses and narratives of nature, protected areas
   and conservation.},
